  "question": {
    "text": "The magnetic field inside a 200 turns solenoid of radius 10 cm is $2.9 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{Tesla}$. If the solenoid carries a current of 0.29 A , then the length of the solenoid is ________ $\\pi \\mathrm{cm}$."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Assuming long solenoid\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{B}=\\mu_0\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{~N}}{\\ell}\\right) \\mathrm{i} \\\\\n& \\ell=\\frac{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{Ni}}{\\mathrm{~B}}=\\frac{\\left(4 \\pi \\times 10^{-7}\\right)(200)(0.29)}{2.9 \\times 10^{-4}} \\mathrm{~m} \\\\\n& =8 \\pi \\mathrm{~cm}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}